            <ArticleTitle>Surgical emphysema and pneumomediastinum complicating dental extraction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>589-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Subcutaneous and mediastinal emphysema is a rare complication of dental extraction and the use of air turbines has often been implicated. We describe a case which highlights a serious complication of the use of an air rotor for the removal of a right second mandibular molar.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
